/*!
 * @mainpage
 * @tableofcontents
 * @section introduction Introduction
 * This documentation combines end user and developer documentation into a 
 * single reference.
 *
 * @section user User manuals
 * These manuals cover topics for end users on how to operate V3FIT.
 * * @ref cl_parsing_sec "Command Line Arguments" Descritptions of the command line arguments.
 * * @ref namelist_sec "V3FIT namelist input file" User manual for the V3FIT namelist input file.
 * * @ref result_file_main "Result output file." User manual for the result NetCDF file.
 *
 * @subsection user_model Model Manual.
 * * @ref model_sec "Model Manual" User manual for the V3FIT model.
 *
 * @subsection user_equilibirum Equilibrium manuals.
 * V3FIT is designed to support many different equilibrium solvers. Currently
 * implemented are two. The VMEC solver and a Vacuum solver.
 *
 * @subsubsection user_vmec_equilibirum VMEC Equilibrium manuals.
 * * <a href="http://vmecwiki.pppl.wikispaces.net"><b>VMEC Wiki</b></a> Information about the VMEC code.
 * * @ref vmec_equilibrium_sec "VMEC Equilibrium Manual" User manual for the VMEC equilibrium.
 *
 * @subsubsection user_vacuum_equilibirum Vacuum Equilibrium manuals.
 * * @ref vacuum_equilibrium_sec "Vacuum Equilibrium Manual" User manual for the Vacuum equilibrium.
 * * @ref vacuum_namelist_sec "Vacuum namelist input file." User manual for the vacuum equilibrium namelist input file.
 *
 * @subsection user_diagnostic Diagnostic input files.
 * Certain diagnostics require input files to describe the diagnostic. Below are
 * documentation for the various files needed to define diagnostics.
 * * @ref sxrem_dot_sec "Soft X-ray Diagnostic Dot File" User manual for the soft x-ray diagnostic dot file.
 * * @ref intpol_dot_sec "Inteferometry/Polarimetry Diagnostic Dot File" User manual for the inteferometry/polarimetry diagnostic dot file.
 * * @ref thomson_dot_sec "Thomson Scattering Diagnostic Dot File" User manual for the Thomson scattering diagnostic dot file.
 *
 * @section programmer Programmer Manuals
 * These manuals are meant to document the various tools and structure used by
 * V3FIT. Reading these pages is not necessary for the operation of V3FIT.
 * * @ref build_system "Build System" Programming manual for the build system using CMake.
 * * @ref doxygen "Doxygen" Manual for the generation of documentation.
 * * @ref architecture "V3FIT Architecture" Programming manual overviewing the design of v3fit.
 * * @ref class_anatomy "V3FIT Class Anatomy" Programming manual describing the structure of class objects.
 * * @ref testing "Testing" Programming manual describing the testing framework.
 */
